{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["And He said, <b>You shall not plow with an ox and a donkey</b>, and the same holds for all kinds of mixed species. And it is a commandment explicitly stated [in] 'Your cattle you shall not mate as mixed species' (Leviticus 19:19), for the way of every worker of his land is to bring his team into one stall and mate them. And He clarified concerning sha'atnez that it is only in wool and linen, and He mentioned 'You shall not wear,' to teach that the prohibition of use is only in the manner of wearing:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Reading אֲסוּרָה as referring to הַעֲלִיָּה (use/benefit); the word וְהִזְכִּיר ('He mentioned') refers to the verse in Leviticus 19:19, 'You shall not wear sha'atnez.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:53:17.839923680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}